  "status": "published",
  "title": "Platform Bed Frame",
  "summary": "A queen platform bed with no box spring needed. Knock-down hardware so it moves house with you.",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "estimatedHours": 12,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "The inside of the frame is 60 1/2 x 80 1/2 in, which gives a standard 60 x 80 in queen mattress 1/4 in of clearance on each side. Cut the 2x8 side rails to 80 1/2 in and the head and foot rails to 60 1/2 in. Cut four 12 in corner legs and two center legs from the 4x4.",
    "Mortise a bed rail fastener into each rail end and its matching plate into the leg face, following the depth on the fastener packet. The rails hook onto the legs, so the frame comes apart without tools.",
    "Glue and screw a 2x2 ledger along the inside of each side rail with its top 2 in below the rail top. The slats sit on these ledgers, leaving the mattress recessed about 1 1/4 in so it cannot slide.",
    "Screw a 2x6 joist hanger to the inside centre of the head rail and the foot rail at ledger height. Cut the 2x6 center beam to fit between them. Screw the two center legs under the beam at the third points, cut so the beam's top lands level with the ledger tops. Check with a straightedge across both ledgers.",
    "Cut fourteen 1x4 slats to 60 1/4 in. Space them evenly so the gaps stay under 3 in, which most mattress warranties require. Fix each end to its ledger and the middle to the beam with one 1 1/4 in screw at each point, so they come out with a driver when you move.",
    "Knock down the frame and sand every part to 120 grit, softening the edges. Apply two coats of water-based polyurethane, sanding lightly between coats.",
    "Reassemble the frame in the bedroom, stick felt pads under the legs, and check that it does not rack before putting the mattress on."
  ],
